[32m+[m[32m## Real-data boundary[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe data package ingests configurable BTS Reporting Carrier On-Time Performance[m
[32m+[m[32mfiles and NOAA/NCEI Global Hourly ISD station observations. BTS schedule, actual[m
[32m+[m[32mtimes, delay outcomes, cancellations, diversions, tail numbers and airport IDs[m
[32m+[m[32mare **observed**. Airport/station matching, timezone-aware operational timestamps,[m
[32m+[m[32mweather features, rotation edges and airport-temporal propagation edges are[m
[32m+[m[32m**derived** from observed data and documented configuration. They are not causal[m
[32m+[m[32mclaims.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe existing hidden-mechanism twin, controlled interventions, and counterfactual[m
[32m+[m[32mground truth remain **synthetic**. Real BTS/NOAA records support future prediction[m
[32m+[m[32mand graph evaluation; they do not prove a causal disruption mechanism. Weather[m
[32m+[m[32malignment is backward-only to scheduled departure, and splits are chronological;[m
[32m+[m[32mdelay outcomes and actual-arrival information are not prediction-time features.[m
[32m+[m
 ## Evaluation plan[m
 [m
 Use disjoint seeds, topology families, disruption locations, and mechanism[m
